The problem asks you to determine: What does this pointer code return?
Node a = new Node(35);
Node b = new Node(10);
Node c = new Node(30);
a.next = b; b.next = c; c.next = null;
Node p = a;
while (p.next != null) p = p.next;
return p.value;

Solve using the information shown. Tracing this code:
int[] a = {3, 6, 8, 10, 15, 18, 21, 22, 26, 28};
int lo = 0, hi = a.length - 1, steps = 0;
while (lo <= hi) { int mid = (lo + hi) / 2; steps++; if (a[mid] == 29) return steps; if (a[mid] < 29) lo = mid + 1; else hi = mid - 1; }
return steps;

Solve using the information shown. What value does this procedure return?
int[] a = {4, 9, 6, -3, 7, 7, 1};
int acc = 1;
for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) if (a[i] != 0) acc *= a[i];
return acc;

